# Candidate integrations for Prime research

This is an entry point to proved constraints and a named occurrence/Need/
quotation assembly. It is not an adopted language or an exhaustive import gate
for every experiment in the subdirectory. Each further integration states its
own assumptions and theorem scope.

Named reusable presentations live outside this directory: `Pure`,
`TypeTheory.CumulativeTower`, `TypeTheory.StagedReflective`, and the
`NeedReferenceSemantics` family. None becomes Prime by existing or by import.
`PrimeCeTTaCurrent` records the separately inspected runtime and calibrations.

Candidate motivation, proof scope, implementation status, and experimental
preference are independent axes. An assembly theorem establishes compatibility
of its components; it does not establish that its choices are necessary or
optimal. See `PrimeCandidates/README.md` for the decision surface.
-/
